<Project>

  <!-- CSJ2K is pruned from every project's restore graph (#25). Excise.Core (vendor/excise) declares
       it as a dependency, but reaches it only from its JPEG 2000 decoder (JpxDecoder.TryDecodeManaged,
       for rendering images inside PDFs someone else made). napkin only writes PDFs and reads back its
       own, which carry no JPEG 2000 image, so nothing napkin runs ever loads CSJ2K: without it the
       package is never restored, never copied beside the build and never shipped. It matters because
       CSJ2K's nuspec names a BSD URL while its repository's licence file is the JJ2000 notice
       (cureos/csj2k, COPYRIGHT-JJ2000-5.1), which grants no right outside JPEG 2000-conforming
       products — a question DESIGN.md §2.1 does not have to answer for a package napkin does not take.
       Pruning does not flow through project references, so it is set here, for every project, rather
       than in Napkin.Interop.Pdf alone. tests/Napkin.Interop.Pdf.Tests/ExciseBoundaryTests holds it:
       no CSJ2K beside the build, and none loaded by writing a page and reading it back.
       docs/third-party-notices.md names it as excluded. -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PrunePackageReference Include="CSJ2K" Version="3.0.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
